From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Sherwin <alex-sherwin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 11:14:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] kitty: untrack placement pins on replace and eviction
 (purrtty patch)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every a=T display step tracks a cursor pin for the new placement, but
neither the same-(image id, placement id) overwrite in addPlacement nor the
eviction path in evictImage ever untracked the pin of the placement being
discarded. A kitty video stream that re-displays one fixed id per frame
leaked ~1 tracked pin per frame without bound: PageList.tracked_pins grows
forever, ~30 PageList operations degrade to O(leaked pins), and when
trackPin eventually fails the display step errors — silently under q=2 —
leaving the freshly stored image with no placement: the video goes
permanently blank while text keeps working.

addImage/addPlacement/evictImage now take the *Screen (the pattern
clearPlacements already uses) and deinit the replaced/evicted placement,
which untracks its pin. Call sites and in-file tests updated.

Verified: zig build test-lib-vt (full suite) green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PKNTeh747EKUC19owSNpYc
